remoteproc: qcom_q6v5: repeated handover is a debug message

Follow-up to q6v5-handover-ratelimit. On SM8450 the SLPI toggles its
handover bit on every sensor sample (issue #46); the folio-state daemon
samples three magnetometer readings per heartbeat, so the message still
reached the console three times a minute, under the ratelimit's burst.
The condition is harmless by design and the handler returns early.
Report it at debug level.

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
index ec5a374ac..c9eb8b027 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
@@ -165,7 +165,7 @@ static irqreturn_t q6v5_handover_interrupt(int irq, void *data)
 	struct qcom_q6v5 *q6v5 = data;
 
 	if (q6v5->handover_issued) {
-		dev_err_ratelimited(q6v5->dev, "Handover signaled, but it already happened\n");
+		dev_dbg(q6v5->dev, "Handover signaled, but it already happened\n");
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 	}
 
